    deps = R_NEWS0 (int, cache->hdr->imagesCount);
    // rest of the code...
} else {
    // handle the case where imagesCount is zero
}
```

So, while the specific vulnerability described in CVE-2021-29604 is not present in the code, a similar issue (null pointer dereference) could occur due to the lack of a check for zero-length arrays. The solution behavior of adding a check to ensure the array size is not zero before using the array can help mitigate this issue.

